    "sticky_notes": [
        {
            "id": "welcome",
            "text": "**Welcome to Vivid!** Three drums, three shapes. Each drum directly triggers its own visual element — nothing is pre-animated. The music IS the animation.",
            "x": -77.00216,
            "y": -768.5166,
            "width": 350.0,
            "height": 100.0,
            "color": 0
        },
        {
            "id": "mapping",
            "text": "**Kick** → big orange circle\n**Snare** → white diamond\n**Hi-hat** → small blue hexagon\n\nEach drum's peak feeds a Smooth (envelope follower), which then drives the shape's scale on both axes — so the shape pulses outward on every hit and decays smoothly between hits.",
            "x": -68.49335,
            "y": -649.12146,
            "width": 320.0,
            "height": 160.0,
            "color": 1
        },
        {
            "id": "envelope_note",
            "text": "**Why Smooth?** A drum's `peak` port is instantaneous — it spikes to ~0.5 for a few milliseconds then collapses. Without smoothing, the shape would flash too briefly to see. Smooth holds the peak (rise=5ms) and decays slowly (fall=400ms) so each hit lingers as a visible pulse.",
            "x": 527.64465,
            "y": -935.4515,
            "width": 340.0,
            "height": 130.0,
            "color": 3
        },
        {
            "id": "try_this",
            "text": "**Try this:** Click the DrumSequencer and toggle steps on/off. Watch how the visuals change instantly. Or change the BPM via the metronome — or change a Smooth's `fall_time` to make pulses decay faster or slower.",
            "x": -97.68874,
            "y": -416.76666,
            "width": 320.0,
            "height": 100.0,
            "color": 2
        }
    ]
